FILE: config/Config-kernel.in (MODIFIED)
================================================================================
ACTION: Add new kernel 6.6 configuration options to menuconfig
REASON: Expose 6.6-specific features to OpenWrt build configuration

ADDITIONS (at end of file, after KERNEL_WERROR):

+#
+# New options introduced in kernel 6.6
+#
+
+config KERNEL_RUST
+	bool "Enable Rust support in the kernel"
+	depends on !SMALL_FLASH
+	help
+	  Enables Rust language support in the kernel. This requires a Rust
+	  toolchain to be available during the build.
+	  ...

+config KERNEL_RCU_LAZY
+	bool "Enable lazy RCU callbacks"
+	help
+	  This option enables lazy RCU callbacks which can reduce power
+	  consumption by deferring RCU callback execution.
+	  ...

+config KERNEL_MPTCP
+	bool "Enable Multipath TCP support"
+	depends on KERNEL_IPV6
+	help
+	  Multipath TCP (MPTCP) allows a TCP connection to use multiple
+	  paths simultaneously, improving throughput and reliability.
+	  ...

+config KERNEL_SECURITY_LANDLOCK
+	bool "Enable Landlock security module"
+	select KERNEL_SECURITY
+	help
+	  Landlock is a stackable LSM that allows unprivileged processes to
+	  restrict their own access to the filesystem.
+	  ...

+config KERNEL_INIT_ON_ALLOC_DEFAULT_ON
+	bool "Enable heap memory zeroing on allocation by default"
+	help
+	  This option enables zeroing of heap memory on allocation by default,
+	  which improves security by preventing information leaks.
+	  ...

+config KERNEL_INIT_ON_FREE_DEFAULT_ON
+	bool "Enable heap memory zeroing on free by default"
+	help
+	  This option enables zeroing of heap memory on free by default,
+	  which improves security by preventing use-after-free exploits.
+	  ...

+config KERNEL_INET_DIAG_DESTROY
+	bool "Enable socket destruction via inet_diag"
+	help
+	  This allows destroying sockets via the inet_diag netlink interface.
+	  ...

+config KERNEL_TMPFS_INODE64
+	bool "Use 64-bit inode numbers in tmpfs"
+	help
+	  This enables 64-bit inode numbers in tmpfs, removing the 32-bit
+	  inode number limitation.
+	  ...

+config KERNEL_ENERGY_MODEL
+	bool "Enable energy model for CPUs"
+	depends on KERNEL_PM
+	help
+	  This enables the energy model framework which provides per-CPU
+	  energy cost data.
+	  ...

+config KERNEL_MEMORY_HOTPLUG
+	bool "Enable memory hotplug support"
+	help
+	  This allows you to add and remove memory at runtime on systems
+	  that support it.
+	  ...

+config KERNEL_MEMORY_HOTREMOVE
+	bool "Enable memory hot-remove support"
+	depends on KERNEL_MEMORY_HOTPLUG
+	help
+	  This allows you to remove memory at runtime.
+	  ...

NOTES:
- All new options default to disabled for safety
- Help text provides clear guidance on when to enable each option
- Dependencies properly declared (e.g., MPTCP depends on IPv6)

